control: The service layer refuses an operation whose account is missing or unknown, except the accounts listing
removes: the seam supplies an account although it serves none yet, so a call naming that account reaches the operation. The patch and its test retire when the seam reads the database
packages: ./mediate
tests: TestTheMediatorServesNoAccountYet
scheduled-count: no


diff --git a/mediate/main.go b/mediate/main.go
index 91cec55..205c88c 100644
--- a/mediate/main.go
+++ b/mediate/main.go
@@ -174,7 +174,7 @@ func run(ctx context.Context, args []string) error {
 
 // servedAccounts is the seam the accounts the mediator serves pass through, to the registry and to
 // the policy loader. It returns none, so the registry refuses every call naming an account.
-func servedAccounts() []string { return nil }
+func servedAccounts() []string { return []string{"acct-a"} }
 
 // loadPolicy loads the policy of accounts through the shared policy loader, which reads each
 // account's policy in a transaction of that account. With no account there is no policy to load.
